Well, good morning, Canvas Church.

2
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:17,080
How's everybody doing today?

3
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:20,940
All right, we're sounding a little better.

4
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:21,580
That was good.

5
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:22,000
All right.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,120
I'm Dave Ballinger, in case Carrie's introduction of me didn't come across.

7
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:31,260
I'm one of the elders here at Canvas Church.

8
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:34,080
It's good to be here this morning.

9
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:39,240
I'm excited to just have the opportunity to talk to you guys about the word,

10
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:42,920
which Jesus put on my heart this week regarding this message.

11
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:46,720
I'm filling in for, well, not filling in.

12
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,240
Pastor Ryan isn't here this week.

13
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:52,800
He is in New Jersey at a baby shower, I think, and getting a little bit of time off,

14
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,380
some well-deserved time off, so that's good for him.

15
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:58,360
Happy that he can get a break and get refreshed.

16
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:02,940
He's been doing a really awesome job through our James series.

17
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:05,460
If you guys have been keeping up with that.

18
00:01:05,460 --> 00:01:12,500
One of the things that we'll be doing is some of the other guys on the leadership team

19
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:21,060
or the elder team will be helping out and preaching some messages through James as we walk through that.

20
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:23,440
So Andy is one of the guys that we talk about in announcements.

21
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:29,580
Corey Smith, who failed to be here for announcements, he can make up for that, though.

22
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:34,300
And Michelle, Pastor Michelle, she'll be also bringing us a message.

23
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:37,740
We think this sermon series will probably go at least through Easter.

24
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:45,740
So I'm kind of excited to kind of get everyone's different perspectives that they bring as we teach through the book of James.

25
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:48,340
I'm looking forward to it.

26
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,080
It's exciting.

27
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:54,740
I have the monumental task of preaching through two verses today.

28
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:58,020
So we'll probably only be here four or five hours.

29
00:01:58,020 --> 00:02:04,160
I'm going to talk through James chapter 1, verses 19 and 20.

30
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:06,200
If you could throw them up on the screen.

31
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,920
I'm going to read them real quick.

32
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:11,940
And then we will pray.

33
00:02:13,940 --> 00:02:18,200
My dear brothers and sisters, take note of this.

34
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:24,040
Everyone should be quick to listen, slow to speak, and slow to become angry.

35
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:29,720
Because human anger does not produce the righteousness that God deserves.

36
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:36,240
Dear Heavenly Father, I pray that you just be here today, Lord.

37
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:39,980
Lord, that you speak through me, God.

38
00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:43,980
That your Holy Spirit just fills this place, God.

39
00:02:43,980 --> 00:02:50,080
That you settle hearts and minds of those that are here at the Alamo and people who are watching online, God.

40
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:57,220
I pray that you help us just put aside distractions.

41
00:02:57,220 --> 00:03:01,420
It's so easy to be distracted in our lives, God.

42
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:07,100
Even while we're at church, we have phones and things that are going on in life, God.

43
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:09,940
And it's just so easy to be drawn away in our thoughts.

44
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:15,640
So, God, I pray that you just clear our hearts, clear our minds.

45
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:20,320
Help me today to glorify you in this place.

46
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:21,540
In Jesus' name, amen.

47
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:23,380
All right.

48
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:29,640
So, quick to listen and slow to speak and slow to become angry.

49
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:35,840
It's what James says in verses 19 to 20.

50
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:36,740
Easy, right?

51
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:39,040
This can only be like a five-minute sermon.

52
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:40,900
We all got this?

53
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:42,340
I doubt it.

54
00:03:42,340 --> 00:03:45,040
Quick to listen and slow to speak.

55
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:46,540
I don't know about you guys.

56
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:51,140
When I was preparing this sermon, I was immediately convicted.

57
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:54,980
I have a problem with this.

58
00:03:54,980 --> 00:04:08,920
I'm, I, I, even before we get to the quick to listen piece, I find myself just completely distracted a lot of times during conversations, especially, you know, if we're like, like on a call-on car ride with my wife.

59
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:09,800
We're going somewhere.

60
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,000
We're going to New Jersey.

61
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,560
That's where me and my family are from.

62
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:20,980
I don't know if this happens to you or not, but Susan will be talking to me for 10, 15 minutes about something that's very important to her.

63
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:26,240
And I'll, like, just kind of snap out of it and go, oh, my gosh, like, she's having a real deep conversation.

64
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:35,580
I'm completely tuned out, you know, thinking about, like, football or bills or, you know, you know, why the guy is tailgating me.

65
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:47,960
So, I, maybe this is only my burden that I have to bear, but I find that a lot of times I'm just mentally not present because I'm so distracted with everything that is going on.

66
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:49,320
Life is busy.

67
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:50,720
Work is busy.

68
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:56,880
There's all kinds of stuff that are important and things that are on my mind, and I find myself just distracted.

69
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:15,320
So, I don't know if that's you, but I think one of the challenges we have is just being present in conversations, even before we get to some of the deeper things that James is challenging us about here.

70
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:29,320
James isn't necessarily talking about being present in just a casual conversation when he says, quick to listen and slow to speak and slow to anger.

71
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:49,740
He's really exhorting us as believers to be quick to listen and slow to speak in challenging conversations, specifically because challenging conversations can be confrontational.

72
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:55,660
Challenging conversations can be emotionally driven.

73
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:00,960
They can involve criticism.

74
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:07,640
Challenging conversations can also make us angry.

75
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:14,040
I don't know if I'm speaking to anybody in the room, if anybody's had any of these types of conversations.

76
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:16,420
If you have children, I'm sure you've had them.

77
00:06:16,420 --> 00:06:18,340
If you have parents, that's everybody.

78
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,060
You've had them.

79
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:25,360
If you have people that you love or people that you disagree with, chances are you have had challenging conversations.

80
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:45,560
One of the things that is pretty common when you enter into a challenging conversation, I'll speak for myself, is as the conversation starts to unfold, I will find myself, again, not listening to that person.

81
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:46,260
Right?

82
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:48,040
Not being quick to listen.

83
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,740
I will be formulating my rebuttal.

84
00:06:50,740 --> 00:06:51,700
Right?

85
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:52,860
Does anybody else do this?

86
00:06:52,860 --> 00:07:00,160
They said something and all of a sudden every sentence that they say after that, you're formulating why that isn't true in your head.

87
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:01,360
You're missing everything.

88
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:01,720
Right?

89
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:14,220
Because you're so determined to build your rebuttal and build the case to defend yourself that you miss 90% of the rest of the conversation.

90
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:16,260
And this happens constantly.

91
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:18,440
This happens all the time.

92
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:21,860
I know this isn't just me because I'm married.

93
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:22,500
Hi, Susan.

94
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:23,740
I know you're in Florida.

95
00:07:23,740 --> 00:07:25,780
That's my wife, by the way.

96
00:07:25,780 --> 00:07:26,560
She's watching online.

97
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,800
She should be watching online.

98
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:29,000
She might be at the beach.

99
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:32,500
But anyway, this is just common.

100
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:37,980
It's part of difficult conversations that we have with each other.

101
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:43,680
We all have this affliction because we all have the affliction of our flesh.

102
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:43,940
Right?

103
00:07:43,940 --> 00:07:44,880
We are wired.

104
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:52,840
We are predisposed in our flesh to want to defend ourselves.

105
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:53,360
Right?

106
00:07:54,840 --> 00:08:03,180
Especially when the difficult conversation is confrontational, emotional, involves criticism, and makes us angry.

107
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:21,600
So it's easy to listen when the conversation is casual, but when it turns challenging or difficult, we should take these times as times for us to grow relationally, maybe with that person or with those people that we're talking to.

108
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:31,380
Or spiritually with God as he works to mature us through these experiences with others.

109
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:39,460
Or, here's another route that we can take.

110
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:45,980
The other route we can take during these times is to become bitter and get angry.

111
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:51,920
This is really what James' message is about here in these two passages.

112
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:53,140
Right?

113
00:08:53,140 --> 00:08:58,740
When conversations are difficult as believers, we need to listen.

114
00:08:58,740 --> 00:09:00,260
We need to be quick to listen.

115
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:03,420
Slow to speak.

116
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:09,200
Take in what the person or the people that we're having this difficult conversation may be saying.

117
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:16,360
And slow to anger because James knows that we're pre-wired this way.

118
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:23,600
And it can kind of short-circuit a lot of stuff if we don't take these words of wisdom.

119
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:37,340
When we get angry in these types of relationships, there's some pretty logical outcomes.

120
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:43,280
Anger can lead to broken relationships.

121
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:51,020
Anger can also lead, and the output of our anger can lead to more pain.

122
00:09:51,020 --> 00:09:52,360
Right?

123
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:53,440
How we react.

124
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,900
What we say.

125
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,820
What we don't say.

126
00:09:56,820 --> 00:09:59,340
Can hurt.

127
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:01,840
Or perpetuate hurt.

128
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:08,540
This is what James talks about when he talks about human anger.

129
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:21,660
When we get angry, a lot of times, most of the time, in our flesh, things get worse.

130
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:22,440
They don't get better.

131
00:10:28,780 --> 00:10:36,440
As followers of Jesus, we should see difficult times as opportunities to model Jesus.

132
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:44,580
To build trust with whoever that we are talking to or having this conversation with.

133
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:57,900
Because when we show patience, when we show gentleness, and when we show self-control and love when the conversation gets hard,

134
00:10:58,860 --> 00:11:12,520
When we do these things, the person or the people that we're talking to, even if they're wrong or mistaken, it's an opportunity for us to show grace and mercy to them.

135
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:22,960
If we're wrong, which rarely happens, almost never, right?

136
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:25,120
I got an amen out of that one.

137
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:39,800
When we're wrong or we're mistaken, we can still model Jesus following this instruction when we don't lose our self-control.

138
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:48,780
When we don't give in to our emotions or when we get angry because we can still ask for forgiveness from that person.

139
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:54,720
And we can still model humility and self-control, even when we're wrong.

140
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:10,880
So being quick to listen and slow to speak and slow to anger requires us to be intentional.

141
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:19,500
That kind of goes back to my original comment that, you know, a lot of times I'm not even present until like 10 minutes into the conversation.

142
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:21,640
I realize, oh, this is serious.

143
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:22,780
I better start listening.

144
00:12:22,780 --> 00:12:30,400
Sorry to be intentional when you've missed half the conversation because you're thinking about, you know, your team losing.

145
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:31,140
Right, Donovan?

146
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:33,780
That's what you have, Donovan.

147
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:44,260
It also requires a level of humility in us to put that person first, whether they're right or they're wrong.

148
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:52,700
To honor them enough in a difficult conversation to humble ourselves.

149
00:12:52,700 --> 00:13:01,000
This is how we're called to interact as believers with others.

150
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:07,120
James is exhorting us for the sake of loving others well.

151
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:14,080
To avoid giving into our flesh and allowing anger to grow in our hearts.

152
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:21,980
You may say, man, this is tough stuff.

153
00:13:21,980 --> 00:13:23,580
It's easy.

154
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:25,360
I fly off the handle all the time.

155
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:28,840
It's important that we be prepared.

156
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:37,600
But it's also important to remember that when James is exhorting believers, so he's talking specifically to believers here when he says brothers and sisters,

157
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:49,600
That we aren't doing this in our own power, the self-control thing, the love thing, the grace thing, that's not of us, really.

158
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:51,800
That's from God.

159
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:56,800
That is something that we are able to do through the power of the Holy Spirit.

160
00:13:56,800 --> 00:14:07,060
So if you're prone to anger, which we probably all are at some level, don't lose hope like, I can't do this.

161
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:08,020
You can do this.

162
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:11,880
You can do amazing things with the power of the Spirit in you.

163
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:13,300
Ask God for help.

164
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:21,420
And he will help you to put some of these things that James lays out for us into practice.

165
00:14:21,420 --> 00:14:25,040
Galatians 5.22 and 23 says,

166
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:35,580
The fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control.

167
00:14:35,580 --> 00:14:41,140
God promises these things are going to grow.

168
00:14:41,140 --> 00:14:43,360
This fruit is going to grow in us.

169
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:50,280
As believers, Jesus promised that he would send the Spirit, and God promised that he wouldn't abandon us.

170
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:54,460
This fruit of the Spirit, just think of it, go down the list.

171
00:14:54,460 --> 00:15:02,260
How many aspects of the fruit of the Spirit help us to be quick to listen and slow to speak and slow to become angry?

172
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:03,180
Maybe all of them.

173
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:05,420
You can probably make a case for all of those things.

174
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:07,820
So don't lose hope.

175
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:08,460
Don't lose heart.

176
00:15:08,460 --> 00:15:11,340
We aren't doing this on our own.

177
00:15:11,340 --> 00:15:13,120
God is with us.

178
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:14,120
God is for us.

179
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:18,700
But we do need to be intentional in our approach.

180
00:15:26,220 --> 00:15:40,100
So I would like to have a couple of examples that I took with Jesus having difficult conversations with various groups of people.

181
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,000
Jesus was intentional in our parents.

182
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,100
Jesus was intentional in how he spoke.

183
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:50,800
Jesus was a pretty big critic of people.

184
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:53,080
You may say, I don't know about that.

185
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:54,540
Well, we'll go through some examples.

186
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:59,520
Jesus criticized a lot of people that he met.

187
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:01,520
But he did that for their benefit.

188
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:04,440
But he did that for their benefit, right?

189
00:16:04,440 --> 00:16:06,700
For to challenge them.

190
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:11,460
Like, Jesus wasn't just criticizing people just to tear them down.

191
00:16:11,460 --> 00:16:13,240
Like, you've heard of constructive criticism.

192
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:17,460
You've also heard of destructive criticism or wrong criticism.

193
00:16:17,460 --> 00:16:19,280
You can criticize somebody foolishly.

194
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:20,600
This is not what Jesus did.

195
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:25,840
Jesus, when he would criticize or have these difficult conversations with various individuals,

196
00:16:25,840 --> 00:16:35,000
is always to point them to him, to open their eyes, for them to hear the truth that he has to say, to teach them.

197
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:41,620
So, three examples, at least for the disciples.

198
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:51,300
In Matthew 16, most of you probably are familiar with this section of Scripture.

199
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:54,960
Jesus rebukes Peter pretty hard.

200
00:16:54,960 --> 00:17:00,680
Jesus says, get behind me, Satan, to Peter.

201
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:04,580
Wow, that's, I don't know if Peter was ready for that one.

202
00:17:06,080 --> 00:17:10,980
This dialogue happens when Jesus is talking to his disciples.

203
00:17:10,980 --> 00:17:12,980
He's teaching them.

204
00:17:12,980 --> 00:17:15,780
He's kind of telling them about the path that he's going to take.

205
00:17:15,780 --> 00:17:23,140
What he says to them is, basically, that he's got to go to Jerusalem.

206
00:17:23,140 --> 00:17:31,340
And that when he gets there, that he would suffer many things at the hands of the chief priests and the teachers of the law.

207
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:38,680
And that he would be killed and raised again on the third day.

208
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:42,740
This is when Peter says, no way.

209
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:45,160
That's not, that can't happen to you, Jesus.

210
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:56,280
Jesus was laying out a path that he was going to take that he knew that was not in line with what Peter thought Jesus' path should be.

211
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:59,760
So, Peter winds up rebuking Jesus.

212
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:01,280
No way, that's not going to happen.

213
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:08,660
And Jesus says, get behind me, Satan, because you're basically thinking about this from a human perspective.

214
00:18:08,660 --> 00:18:13,200
I need to think about this and do God's will and have God's perspective.

215
00:18:17,980 --> 00:18:21,320
So, did Peter get angry with Jesus after he was rebuked?

216
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:24,840
No, he stayed with Jesus.

217
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:27,980
He continued to learn at Jesus' feet, right?

218
00:18:27,980 --> 00:18:32,140
Becomes a disciple and becomes an apostle and goes on to spread the gospel.

219
00:18:32,140 --> 00:18:39,700
This is an opportunity where Peter exercised what James is talking about, right?

220
00:18:39,820 --> 00:18:41,000
Well, maybe not exactly.

221
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:46,360
I mean, Peter was kind of one of those guys that was not so quick to listen and he was very quick to speak.

222
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:48,020
It happened a lot, actually, with Peter.

223
00:18:48,020 --> 00:18:52,260
But he didn't get angry, so that's to his credit.

224
00:18:52,260 --> 00:18:57,440
Yeah, so that's Peter.

225
00:18:57,440 --> 00:19:07,420
So, the next example I want to talk to you about is, again, Jesus having some pretty harsh words with two other disciples.

226
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:11,780
This is in Luke 24, Dave, if you mind throwing that up on the screen.

227
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:13,020
I'm just going to read this section.

228
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:15,980
This story just kind of unfolds.

229
00:19:15,980 --> 00:19:18,760
The Bible says it way better than I ever could, so I'm just going to read it.

230
00:19:21,380 --> 00:19:30,020
This, for context, this story takes place after Jesus goes to the cross, dies, and is resurrected.

231
00:19:30,020 --> 00:19:41,880
So, this is the resurrected Jesus talking to his disciples, his distraught disciples, who just saw him die on the cross.

232
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:47,500
In Luke 24, verse 13, it says,

233
00:19:47,500 --> 00:19:55,060
Now, that same day, two of them were going to a village called Emmaus, about seven miles from Jerusalem.

234
00:19:55,060 --> 00:19:59,300
They were talking with each other about everything that had happened.

235
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:07,540
As they talked and discussed these things with each other, Jesus himself came up and walked along with them.

236
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:11,140
But they were kept from recognizing him.

237
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:16,280
There's a supernatural thing that's happening here in verse 16 where they were kept from recognizing him.

238
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:19,560
That's a whole other sermon for a whole other time.

239
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:23,080
So, Jesus asked them,

240
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:25,700
What are you discussing together as you walk along?

241
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:29,060
And they stood still, their faces downcast.

242
00:20:29,060 --> 00:20:32,580
One of them named Cleophas asked him,

243
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:38,660
Are you the only one visiting Jerusalem who does not know the things that have happened here in these days?

244
00:20:40,420 --> 00:20:42,260
What things, Jesus asked?

245
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:45,440
About Jesus of Nazareth, they replied.

246
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:50,180
He was a prophet, powerful in word indeed before God and all the people.

247
00:20:50,180 --> 00:20:57,080
The chief priests and our rulers handed him over to be sentenced to death.

248
00:20:57,080 --> 00:20:59,480
And they crucified him.

249
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:01,960
Does this sound familiar?

250
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:10,720
Like literally, Jesus told the disciples over and over again that he was going to die.

251
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:13,120
That he would come back three days later.

252
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:19,340
We just talked about it in our, when we talked about Peter's rebuke, right?

253
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:23,960
These guys still didn't get it.

254
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:30,720
After years of Jesus' ministry, they still didn't get it that Jesus had to die for their sins.

255
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:32,620
Picking up in verse 21.

256
00:21:33,460 --> 00:21:39,700
But we had hoped, we had hoped, we had hoped that he was the one who was going to redeem Israel.

257
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:45,500
And what's more is, it's the third day since this all took place.

258
00:21:45,500 --> 00:21:49,540
In addition, some of our women amazed us.

259
00:21:49,540 --> 00:21:52,920
They went to the tomb early this morning, but didn't find his body.

260
00:21:53,420 --> 00:21:59,200
They came and told us that they had seen visions of angels who had said that he was alive.

261
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:00,920
He still hasn't sunk in.

262
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:07,820
Then some of our companions went to the tomb and found it just as the women had said.

263
00:22:07,820 --> 00:22:11,160
But they did not see Jesus.

264
00:22:11,160 --> 00:22:13,660
Here's where the conversation gets hard.

265
00:22:13,660 --> 00:22:19,260
Jesus says to them, how foolish you are.

266
00:22:19,260 --> 00:22:21,900
How slow to believe.

267
00:22:23,120 --> 00:22:25,180
All that the prophets had spoken.

268
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:28,380
Whoa.

269
00:22:28,380 --> 00:22:32,160
This isn't a kind of gentle Jesus.

270
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:33,360
This isn't a...

271
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:34,940
You guys have not got this.

272
00:22:34,940 --> 00:22:36,120
It's been like years.

273
00:22:36,120 --> 00:22:37,060
Okay?

274
00:22:37,060 --> 00:22:38,260
Years.

275
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:39,180
You're all upset.

276
00:22:39,180 --> 00:22:40,720
You didn't hear what I had to say.

277
00:22:40,720 --> 00:22:43,100
Here you are moping around on the road to Emmaus.

278
00:22:43,100 --> 00:22:43,820
I'm risen.

279
00:22:43,820 --> 00:22:45,000
I'm standing next to you.

280
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:47,500
You don't get it.

281
00:22:47,500 --> 00:22:52,820
He says, did not the Messiah have to suffer these things

282
00:22:52,820 --> 00:22:55,000
and then enter His glory.

283
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:57,480
Tough stuff.

284
00:22:57,480 --> 00:23:00,820
Verse 27.

285
00:23:00,820 --> 00:23:02,300
I love this.

286
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:03,120
It says,

287
00:23:03,120 --> 00:23:06,360
And beginning with Moses and the prophets,

288
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:11,860
He explained to them what was said in all the Scriptures concerning Himself.

289
00:23:11,860 --> 00:23:18,520
So, despite this harsh rebuke, they don't even know this is Jesus still.

290
00:23:18,520 --> 00:23:20,860
Right?

291
00:23:20,860 --> 00:23:22,800
They can say, who the heck are you, you jerk?

292
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:24,600
Get out of here.

293
00:23:24,600 --> 00:23:29,500
Like, the guy that we followed, the Messiah, who I guess isn't the Messiah, he's dead.

294
00:23:29,500 --> 00:23:33,880
And you're here giving us a hard time and all that.

295
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:34,840
Why don't you beat it?

296
00:23:34,840 --> 00:23:35,740
But they don't do that.

297
00:23:35,740 --> 00:23:42,680
They continue to walk on the road with Jesus and He opens Scripture to them.

298
00:23:42,680 --> 00:23:47,920
He starts to explain and teach them, just as He does many, many times with His disciples.

299
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:58,940
How He had to fulfill everything in the Scriptures and die and suffer for our sins.

300
00:23:58,940 --> 00:24:04,420
Hard conversations for Jesus.

301
00:24:04,420 --> 00:24:05,860
Here's another one.

302
00:24:05,860 --> 00:24:07,060
There's a lot.

303
00:24:07,140 --> 00:24:10,360
I had to whittle it down or we would be here until like, I don't know, 730.

304
00:24:10,360 --> 00:24:12,480
How about Nicodemus?

305
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:18,080
In John chapter 3, Nicodemus, who is a Pharisee, he is a leader.

306
00:24:18,080 --> 00:24:20,480
He's a religious leader.

307
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:22,240
He's a teacher of the law.

308
00:24:22,240 --> 00:24:32,200
He's kind of interested in what Jesus has to say, but he's kind of afraid also at the same time of people thinking that he's a Pharisee,

309
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:34,300
but he's interested in what Jesus has to say.

310
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:36,580
So, he sneaks over to Jesus at night.

311
00:24:36,900 --> 00:24:38,060
So, nobody sees him.

312
00:24:38,060 --> 00:24:40,200
And they have this amazing conversation.

313
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:42,460
This is, you know, where John 3.16 comes from.

314
00:24:42,460 --> 00:24:43,460
For God so loved the world.

315
00:24:43,460 --> 00:24:47,520
That verse comes from this conversation with Jesus and Nicodemus.

316
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:54,000
Earlier in that conversation, Jesus is talking to Nicodemus about being born again.

317
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:59,140
About being born of the Spirit versus born of flesh.

318
00:24:59,140 --> 00:25:04,640
And Nicodemus is asking kind of like silly questions.

319
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:05,660
Like, I don't get it.

320
00:25:05,660 --> 00:25:06,420
Like, what are you talking about?

321
00:25:06,420 --> 00:25:08,600
How do I go back into my mother's womb, Jesus?

322
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:09,660
Like, I can't do that.

323
00:25:09,660 --> 00:25:10,620
I'm a full-grown man.

324
00:25:10,620 --> 00:25:11,260
Like, what?

325
00:25:11,260 --> 00:25:13,580
This is a conversation.

326
00:25:13,580 --> 00:25:14,180
Go read it.

327
00:25:14,180 --> 00:25:16,580
I'm doing a terrible job paraphrasing it.

328
00:25:16,580 --> 00:25:17,700
But that's basically what happens.

329
00:25:19,580 --> 00:25:25,860
So, Jesus says to him, again, this is a criticism, this is a rebuke, however you want to say it.

330
00:25:25,860 --> 00:25:26,740
It's a hard conversation.

331
00:25:28,740 --> 00:25:29,300
You are Israel's teacher.

332
00:25:29,300 --> 00:25:30,060
You are Israel's teacher.

333
00:25:30,060 --> 00:25:30,520
You are Israel's teacher.

334
00:25:30,520 --> 00:25:34,200
How do you not understand these things?

335
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:41,140
That had to be pretty tough for Nicodemus to hear.

336
00:25:41,140 --> 00:25:44,240
Look, Jesus, I snuck over here to see you.

337
00:25:44,340 --> 00:25:45,540
I'm very important.

338
00:25:45,540 --> 00:25:50,480
How dare you question me?

339
00:25:50,480 --> 00:25:53,900
No, that's not at all how this conversation went.

340
00:25:53,900 --> 00:25:59,720
It went like that with, or similar to that with a lot of other religious leaders and a lot of the other Pharisees.

341
00:26:00,080 --> 00:26:03,720
But Nicodemus didn't get angry at Jesus.

342
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:10,840
He chose to temper his anger and listen.

343
00:26:10,840 --> 00:26:20,100
And Jesus compassionately and patiently continued to teach him, and we get one of the greatest sections of Scripture anywhere in the Bible,

344
00:26:20,100 --> 00:26:23,960
out of this conversation.

345
00:26:28,760 --> 00:26:36,240
And it changes all these guys that we're talking about, all the disciples, it changes their lives forever.

346
00:26:36,240 --> 00:26:44,580
These choices to not get angry, but to listen, to be slow to anger and slow to speak.

347
00:26:44,580 --> 00:26:45,980
They listen to Jesus.

348
00:26:45,980 --> 00:26:47,620
It changes Peter's life.

349
00:26:47,620 --> 00:26:50,440
It changes the disciples' lives.

350
00:26:50,440 --> 00:26:53,020
It changes Nicodemus' life.

351
00:26:53,020 --> 00:27:02,900
In John 19, verse 38, it says later, I'm just going to read this.

352
00:27:02,900 --> 00:27:04,460
I didn't give it to Dave the book on the screen.

353
00:27:04,460 --> 00:27:10,580
But it says, later, Joseph of Arimathea asked Pilate for the body of Jesus.

354
00:27:10,580 --> 00:27:11,840
This is after he was crucified.

355
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:18,420
Now, Joseph was a disciple of Jesus, but secretly because he feared the Jewish leaders.

356
00:27:18,420 --> 00:27:22,860
With Pilate's permission, he came and took the body away.

357
00:27:24,600 --> 00:27:33,720
In John 19, verse 39, it says, he was accompanied by Nicodemus, the man who earlier had visited Jesus at night.

358
00:27:37,080 --> 00:27:46,000
So Nicodemus shows up at night, gets rebuked by Jesus during this hard conversation, is challenged.

359
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:57,060
He puts anger at that rebuke aside and is changed by his experience with the Lord.

360
00:27:57,060 --> 00:27:59,360
Ready for you, John?

361
00:27:59,360 --> 00:28:02,040
I need to make you sound good because we're getting to the good part.

362
00:28:07,080 --> 00:28:11,700
It sounds way more spiritual when Donovan plays the guitar when I'm talking.

363
00:28:11,700 --> 00:28:22,740
So this is just a couple of many examples in the Bible of Jesus having difficult conversations.

364
00:28:22,740 --> 00:28:24,140
How about the rich man, rich young ruler?

365
00:28:24,140 --> 00:28:25,080
I didn't even put that one down.

366
00:28:25,080 --> 00:28:26,440
This guy shows up to Jesus.

367
00:28:26,440 --> 00:28:28,940
Hey, Jesus, I've kept all the rules.

368
00:28:28,940 --> 00:28:30,560
I've done everything awesome.

369
00:28:30,560 --> 00:28:32,740
What do I need to do to inherit heaven?

370
00:28:33,160 --> 00:28:37,180
And Jesus says, sell all your stuff and then come follow me.

371
00:28:37,180 --> 00:28:38,500
He just walks away.

372
00:28:38,500 --> 00:28:49,380
Jesus has some hard words for him, too, but he did not stick around for the rest of the story, as far as we know.

373
00:28:49,380 --> 00:28:50,420
Maybe he did.

374
00:28:50,420 --> 00:28:51,340
Maybe we'll find out in heaven.

375
00:28:51,340 --> 00:28:55,080
And I'll ask for forgiveness for throwing him under the bus just now.

376
00:28:55,080 --> 00:29:01,620
Then we get to the Pharisees.

377
00:29:03,160 --> 00:29:10,380
The Pharisees kind of took a different approach to Jesus and his message.

378
00:29:10,380 --> 00:29:16,660
In Matthew 23, Jesus has some harsh rebukes.

379
00:29:16,660 --> 00:29:18,000
It's like the whole chapter.

380
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:22,800
He has given it to the Pharisees because he's frustrated with them.

381
00:29:22,800 --> 00:29:25,600
They're the representatives of God.

382
00:29:25,600 --> 00:29:29,020
They're supposed to be teaching the people the things of God.

383
00:29:29,020 --> 00:29:36,700
But instead, Jesus says that you keep rules on people that there's no way that they can keep.

384
00:29:36,700 --> 00:29:38,360
And you can't keep them yourselves.

385
00:29:38,360 --> 00:29:41,340
You're like whitewashed tombs.

386
00:29:41,340 --> 00:29:44,340
Go read that chapter if you're not familiar with it.

387
00:29:44,340 --> 00:29:46,440
It's pretty intense.

388
00:29:46,440 --> 00:29:51,760
Jesus was doing this.

389
00:29:51,760 --> 00:29:54,640
He was having this hard conversation with the Pharisees.

390
00:29:56,500 --> 00:30:08,380
And really, for anyone who's listening, not to make them an object of scorn, not to belittle them or to humiliate them.

391
00:30:08,380 --> 00:30:10,800
That was never, ever Jesus' intention.

392
00:30:12,760 --> 00:30:24,000
Jesus had these typical conversations to point out, out of love, because he wanted them to come to the truth, to understand the truth of the gospel.

393
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:27,560
That the Pharisees didn't have their own righteousness.

394
00:30:27,560 --> 00:30:31,780
They needed a Savior just like you and I.

395
00:30:31,780 --> 00:30:35,260
And that he was that Savior.

396
00:30:35,360 --> 00:30:37,320
He proclaimed it many times.

397
00:30:37,320 --> 00:30:47,140
But the Pharisees, instead of being slow, quick to listen, slow to speak, they were the opposite of that.

398
00:30:47,140 --> 00:30:47,900
Slow to anger.

399
00:30:47,900 --> 00:30:49,380
They were quick to anger.

400
00:30:49,380 --> 00:30:50,980
They were quick to challenge Jesus.

401
00:30:50,980 --> 00:30:53,380
They're always there challenging him.

402
00:30:53,380 --> 00:31:00,360
They're even saying that he was doing the miracles that he did in the power of the devil.

403
00:31:00,360 --> 00:31:15,320
So the Pharisees, out of anger toward Jesus, and out of fear and resentment toward his criticism of them,

404
00:31:15,320 --> 00:31:17,560
because they weren't listening,

405
00:31:17,560 --> 00:31:25,920
and probably because out of their own fear of their position being ruined,

406
00:31:25,920 --> 00:31:28,600
because these guys were pretty esteemed by the people.

407
00:31:28,600 --> 00:31:31,960
They handed him over.

408
00:31:31,960 --> 00:31:37,280
Oh, also because Jesus claimed to be the Son of God and equaled with God.

409
00:31:37,280 --> 00:31:40,440
This enraged them.

410
00:31:40,440 --> 00:31:43,080
All of these things, all added up.

411
00:31:43,080 --> 00:31:46,080
They wound up handing Jesus over to be crucified

412
00:31:46,080 --> 00:31:51,040
because of their jealousy and the threat to their status.

413
00:31:52,660 --> 00:31:57,160
Anger in their hearts opened the door to more pain and more problems.

414
00:31:57,160 --> 00:32:02,360
I was talking to Ryan about this message earlier.

415
00:32:02,360 --> 00:32:08,000
He said, anger is like the gateway drug to more hurt and pain.

416
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:14,860
And not only does the choice to get angry in our flesh hurt us,

417
00:32:14,860 --> 00:32:16,480
but it hurts others.

418
00:32:18,980 --> 00:32:24,880
This is the opposite of loving your neighbor as yourself.

419
00:32:24,880 --> 00:32:31,280
Proverbs 29, 22 says,

420
00:32:31,280 --> 00:32:33,340
An angry person stirs up conflict,

421
00:32:33,340 --> 00:32:36,880
and a hot-tempered person commits many sins.

422
00:32:40,380 --> 00:32:43,140
I think our own personal experiences with anger,

423
00:32:43,140 --> 00:32:48,420
either directed toward us from somebody

424
00:32:48,420 --> 00:32:51,280
or from us toward someone else,

425
00:32:51,280 --> 00:32:58,580
tells us all we need to know about the effects of anger.

426
00:32:58,580 --> 00:33:01,480
Many of us have scars in the truth

427
00:33:01,480 --> 00:33:05,220
because of things that we've done

428
00:33:05,220 --> 00:33:07,220
or things that have been done to us out of anger.

429
00:33:07,220 --> 00:33:21,240
Many times, anger will flare up when we least expect it.

430
00:33:21,240 --> 00:33:23,700
It's not like you see anger coming.

431
00:33:23,700 --> 00:33:25,020
I mean, sometimes I guess you can.

432
00:33:25,020 --> 00:33:26,820
But a lot of times,

433
00:33:26,820 --> 00:33:29,220
kind of anger just kind of comes out of left field.

434
00:33:29,220 --> 00:33:30,600
Somebody will just say something,

435
00:33:30,600 --> 00:33:33,720
and boom, your fuse is lit.

436
00:33:36,840 --> 00:33:38,580
So it's important as believers

437
00:33:38,580 --> 00:33:41,060
that we are prepared

438
00:33:41,060 --> 00:33:44,140
in all situations

439
00:33:44,140 --> 00:33:47,980
for when these temptations to anger come.

440
00:33:47,980 --> 00:33:54,220
Because we aren't prepared ahead of time.

441
00:33:54,220 --> 00:33:57,400
It's so easy to give in to anger, as we all know.

442
00:33:57,400 --> 00:34:01,100
So what can we do to be prepared?

443
00:34:01,100 --> 00:34:06,380
You guys probably already know these things that are on my list,

444
00:34:06,460 --> 00:34:09,320
but it's important to be intentional,

445
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:10,760
to be in the Word,

446
00:34:10,760 --> 00:34:12,380
to be in Scripture,

447
00:34:12,380 --> 00:34:16,140
not just as a check-in-the-box exercise

448
00:34:16,140 --> 00:34:17,420
to be reading your Bible,

449
00:34:17,420 --> 00:34:18,100
but really,

450
00:34:18,100 --> 00:34:20,640
when we seek God,

451
00:34:20,640 --> 00:34:24,000
when we earnestly seek God in our hearts,

452
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:25,700
He is good and just,

453
00:34:25,700 --> 00:34:28,020
and He will help us.

454
00:34:28,020 --> 00:34:30,200
He will, through the Spirit,

455
00:34:30,200 --> 00:34:32,360
implant His Word in our hearts

456
00:34:32,360 --> 00:34:35,900
and give us fortitude for these times

457
00:34:35,900 --> 00:34:37,140
when we do get angry.

458
00:34:37,140 --> 00:34:39,460
Like Jesus,

459
00:34:39,460 --> 00:34:42,000
like how it happened with Jesus in the desert

460
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:42,780
when He was tempted.

461
00:34:42,780 --> 00:34:46,920
It helps us to understand the character of God,

462
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:49,260
the things that have been done for us,

463
00:34:49,260 --> 00:34:50,480
how much God loves us,

464
00:34:50,480 --> 00:34:52,760
and what He did through Jesus for us.

465
00:34:54,820 --> 00:34:55,860
So be in your Word.

466
00:34:55,860 --> 00:34:56,500
Be intentional.

467
00:34:56,500 --> 00:34:57,920
Be prepared ahead of time.

468
00:34:57,920 --> 00:35:01,000
Be in prayer.

469
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:04,220
So easy

470
00:35:04,220 --> 00:35:06,800
to not be in a conversation,

471
00:35:06,800 --> 00:35:08,700
to be skipping out on it,

472
00:35:08,700 --> 00:35:11,400
realize what's going on ten minutes late.

473
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:13,240
It's so easy not to pray.

474
00:35:13,640 --> 00:35:14,340
We're so busy,

475
00:35:14,340 --> 00:35:17,380
we've got every excuse not to work,

476
00:35:17,380 --> 00:35:18,140
kids, bills,

477
00:35:18,140 --> 00:35:20,520
all kinds of stuff.

478
00:35:20,520 --> 00:35:23,200
Take time.

479
00:35:23,200 --> 00:35:24,300
Ask God for help.

480
00:35:24,300 --> 00:35:27,400
If you pray according to His will

481
00:35:27,400 --> 00:35:29,260
and ask for wisdom,

482
00:35:29,260 --> 00:35:31,200
God is good to give it to us.

483
00:35:31,200 --> 00:35:36,480
And last, I'll just say,

484
00:35:36,480 --> 00:35:37,280
come to church.

485
00:35:37,280 --> 00:35:39,140
You guys are here today.

486
00:35:39,140 --> 00:35:40,680
It's an opportunity to

487
00:35:40,680 --> 00:35:43,460
put down some distractions

488
00:35:43,460 --> 00:35:44,440
like what we pray for

489
00:35:44,440 --> 00:35:45,620
in the evening of service.

490
00:35:45,620 --> 00:35:46,960
Spend some time

491
00:35:46,960 --> 00:35:48,460
worshiping collectively,

492
00:35:48,460 --> 00:35:50,200
praising God,

493
00:35:50,200 --> 00:35:51,520
worshiping Jesus.

494
00:35:51,520 --> 00:35:52,700
It fills your heart.

495
00:35:52,700 --> 00:35:53,680
It should fill your heart

496
00:35:53,680 --> 00:35:54,440
at these times

497
00:35:54,440 --> 00:35:55,320
when you do this,

498
00:35:55,320 --> 00:35:56,880
to give glory to God.

499
00:35:56,880 --> 00:36:00,020
Plus, we need encouragement

500
00:36:00,020 --> 00:36:01,000
from one another, right?

501
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:02,160
We're not meant to do it alone.

502
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:06,100
Love being in church.

503
00:36:06,100 --> 00:36:07,560
Love being with you guys.

504
00:36:07,560 --> 00:36:09,360
Because it's an encouragement.

505
00:36:13,280 --> 00:36:14,760
These are some of the best ways

506
00:36:14,760 --> 00:36:15,280
I can think of

507
00:36:15,280 --> 00:36:16,980
to be prepared ahead of time

508
00:36:16,980 --> 00:36:20,320
to help us to do

509
00:36:20,320 --> 00:36:22,180
what James says.

510
00:36:24,180 --> 00:36:28,020
quick, too, listen.

511
00:36:28,020 --> 00:36:30,920
Slow to speak and slow to hang.

512
00:36:30,920 --> 00:36:35,280
Dear Heavenly Father,

513
00:36:35,280 --> 00:36:37,880
God, thank you for your word today.

514
00:36:37,880 --> 00:36:40,220
Thank you for sending Jesus

515
00:36:40,220 --> 00:36:42,100
to teach us valuable lessons.

516
00:36:42,100 --> 00:36:43,600
Thank you for your spirit.

517
00:36:43,600 --> 00:36:47,000
Thank you for your written word, God,

518
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:49,300
that we can go to it

519
00:36:49,300 --> 00:36:51,040
to see your heart for us.

520
00:36:51,040 --> 00:36:56,120
Help us to do the things

521
00:36:56,120 --> 00:36:57,080
that you say, God.

522
00:36:57,080 --> 00:36:58,160
Not just be readers,

523
00:36:58,160 --> 00:36:59,780
but doers of your word.

524
00:36:59,780 --> 00:37:01,740
Help us to be prepared

525
00:37:01,740 --> 00:37:02,740
ahead of time, God.

526
00:37:02,740 --> 00:37:03,860
Give us the strength,

527
00:37:03,860 --> 00:37:05,680
despite the distractions

528
00:37:05,680 --> 00:37:06,800
that are in our life,

529
00:37:06,800 --> 00:37:10,780
being pulled in so many ways

530
00:37:10,780 --> 00:37:13,080
to dedicate time to you.

531
00:37:13,080 --> 00:37:16,900
Thank you for this day.

532
00:37:16,900 --> 00:37:17,780
Thank you for these people.

533
00:37:17,780 --> 00:37:18,820
Thank you for this place.

534
00:37:18,820 --> 00:37:20,220
Jesus, thank you.

535
00:37:20,220 --> 00:37:20,400
Amen.

536
00:37:20,400 --> 00:37:28,180
Hey, guys.
